4. Share-alike: changes must be published as open source

   If You distribute a Derivative, or let other people interact with a
   Derivative over a network (for example by hosting a modified server or
   offering a modified client), You must:

   a. publish the complete corresponding source code of the Derivative,
      including your changes, build scripts and configuration needed to run it,
      to the public at no charge, in a form people can freely download;
   b. license the Derivative to everyone under this same license, with no
      additional restrictions;
   c. keep all notices, and mark your changes clearly with the date and your
      name;
   d. never close, withhold or make private any part of a Derivative that You
      have already distributed or run for others.

   Changes You make and keep entirely private, used only by You, do not need to
   be published. Separate programs that merely talk to Cove through its
   documented public APIs (for example bots) are not Derivatives.

